# Privacy / telemetry settings for this build. Read by run.sh, so it applies to both
# ./run.sh and ./run-openai.sh. Telemetry is OFF BY DEFAULT: it stays disabled even if this
# file is missing or blank. Set DISABLE_TELEMETRY=0 to explicitly opt back IN to the app's
# stock telemetry behavior. See ANTHROPIC_ENDPOINTS.md for the full traffic list.
#
# DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1 -> turn OFF all telemetry & analytics. Three levers are needed,
# because the app has three independent telemetry paths:
#
#  1. Bundled Claude Code agent — respects the standard env vars, so run.sh exports
#     DISABLE_TELEMETRY, DO_NOT_TRACK, CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC.
#
#  2. Desktop shell (Electron main) — does NOT respect those env vars. It gates on the
#     managed config Me().telemetry.disable{Nonessential,NonessentialServices,Essential},
#     which is only settable from a root-owned MDM plist in /Library/Managed Preferences.
#     So run.sh exports PRIVACY_DISABLE_TELEMETRY and env-gated patches in
#     app/.vite/build/index.chunk-CnWKsyE_.js force those gates on. That silences the
#     [EventLogging] flusher (claude.ai /api/event_logging/v2/batch), nonessential
#     services, and Sentry, and cancels telemetry-PATH requests (/api/event_logging,
#     the OTLP /v1/logs|traces|metrics exporter, and a.claude.ai/isolated-segment.html)
#     which ride first-party or admin-configured hosts and therefore cannot be blocked
#     by hostname.
#
#  3. Remote claude.ai web app in the renderer — its Datadog RUM + Sentry are loaded
#     from assets-proxy.anthropic.com and consult none of the above, so run.sh
#     DNS-sinkholes their dedicated hosts via Chromium --host-resolver-rules.
#
#     A vendor-domain blocklist alone is NOT enough here, because some of this analytics
#     is FIRST-PARTY PROXIED onto anthropic.com subdomains (found by auditing real
#     traffic, not the bundle — none of it is called from local code):
#       s-cdn.anthropic.com  /s.js + /images/<n>.gif?<session,user,…>  tracker + pixels
#       a-cdn.anthropic.com  /v1/projects/<writeKey>/settings, Amplitude plugin bundles
#                            — this is Segment's analytics.js, so "*segment.com" MISSES it
#       a-api.anthropic.com  /v1/b (Segment batch), /v1/m                event ingest
#     These are sinkholed by EXACT hostname (a "*anthropic.com" pattern would also kill
#     api.anthropic.com inference and assets-proxy.anthropic.com app code) AND added to
#     the lever-2 canceller, because DNS blocking does not stop a CACHED script: the
#     analytics bundles were verified being served from HTTP_CACHE_READ_DATA with zero
#     network events, whereas webRequest cancellation runs before the cache lookup.
#
# NOT blocked, deliberately: a.claude.ai/cdn-cgi/challenge-platform (Cloudflare bot
# management — security infrastructure; blocking risks challenges/lockout) and
# api.github.com (the app's functional GitHub integration). Claims that this app calls
# Intercom, DoubleClick/Google Ads or the Meta Pixel did NOT reproduce: zero requests to
# any of them across full 90s runs. Any such cookies in the profile came from browsing
# claude.ai web pages, not from desktop traffic.
#
# Verified with --log-net-log over 90s runs: [EventLogging] flushes 0 (was 56), app logs
# "Sentry disabled (disableEssentialTelemetry)", isolated-segment.html is
# ERR_BLOCKED_BY_CLIENT, datadog 68 attempts -> ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED / 0 bytes, and
# s-cdn/a-cdn/a-api/sentry/event_logging at 0 requests and 0 bytes — while
# api.anthropic.com (1.6MB), assets-proxy (5.4MB), claude.ai app APIs (722KB) and the
# GitHub integration all still work and the app stays logged in. Control-tested at
# DISABLE_TELEMETRY=0: telemetry returns.
DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1
